// Rule 4: host goes silent
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Finding:        Every log source went quiet from 12:27 to 13:43 UTC. Audit
//                 serial numbers and process IDs reset when logging returned,
//                 which points to a host restart, not a stopped forwarder.
//                 Nothing alerted on the loss of collection.
// Data source:    Sysmon for Linux, auditd and Apache access log
//                 (HartwellSysmon_CL, HartwellAudit_CL, HartwellApache_CL),
//                 Microsoft Sentinel, counted in 5-minute bins.
// Time column:    OriginalTime (TimeGenerated is ingestion time in this data).
// Hunt window:    2026-10-23 04:00 to 16:00 UTC.
// Result:         15 silent 5-minute bins. 14 of them, from 12:30 to 13:35,
//                 are the restart. One bin at 04:25 is unexplained.
// What it missed: The cause. The rule fires on the silence, not on why it
//                 happened. The counters on either side of the gap are what
//                 show it was a restart.
// Expected false positives: Planned maintenance and patch reboots. Suppress
//                 during change windows.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
union HartwellSysmon_CL, HartwellAudit_CL, HartwellApache_CL
| make-series Events=count() default=0 on OriginalTime from datetime(2026-10-23T04:00:00Z) to datetime(2026-10-23T16:00:00Z) step 5m
| mv-expand OriginalTime to typeof(datetime), Events to typeof(long)
| where Events == 0
| summarize SilentBins=count(), First=min(OriginalTime), Last=max(OriginalTime)
